{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0156fWcML5FqUdx25JJ2SgGR","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t \"number\": 70,\n3\t \"title\": \"GPU subprocess crash (STATUS_BREAKPOINT / exit_code=-2147483645) on Intel Iris Xe Tiger Lake\",\n4\t \"body\": \"### Preflight Checklist\\n\\n- [x] I have read the [Contributing Guidelines](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) for this project.\\n- [x] I agree to follow the [Code of Conduct](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) that this project adheres to.\\n- [x] I have searched the [issue tracker](https://www.github.com/electron/electron/issues) for a bug report that matches the one I want to file, without success.\\n\\n### Electron Version\\n\\nShipped with Signal Desktop 8.26.0 (Electron 32.x range)\\n\\n### What operating system(s) are you using?\\n\\nWindows\\n\\n### Operating System Version\\n\\nShipped with Signal Desktop 8.26.0 (Electron 32.x range)\\n\\n### What arch are you using?\\n\\nx64\\n\\n### Last Known Working Electron version\\n\\nUnknown\\n\\n### Does the issue also appear in Chromium / Google Chrome?\\n\\nI don't know how to test\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nSignal Desktop (and other Electron apps) should start normally with a visible window and working renderer.\\n\\n### Actual Behavior\\n\\nSignal silently crashes at startup with no window shown. The GPU subprocess exits with `STATUS_BREAKPOINT` (`0x80000003` / exit code `-2147483645`). This is a related but distinct variant from the original reports in #32440 which showed `STATUS_ACCESS_VIOLATION` (`0xC0000005`).\\n\\nWindows Application Event Log (Event ID 1000):\\n```text\\nFaulting application: Signal.exe\\nException code: 0x80000003 (STATUS_BREAKPOINT)\\nFault offset: 0x0000000006fefb69  ← identical across every crash attempt\\n```\\n\\nRunning with `--disable-gpu` surfaces the GPU subprocess crash explicitly:\\n```text\\n[ERROR:gpu_process_host.cc:1108] GPU process exited unexpectedly: exit_code=-2147483645\\n[FATAL:gpu_data_manager_impl_private.cc:416] GPU process isn't usable. Goodbye.\\n```\\n\\n**Secondary issue:** Even after working around the startup crash with `--in-process-gpu`, newly spawned renderer processes (e.g. Help → About window) crash with the same exit code:\\n```text\\nRender process is gone\\nError: Reason: crashed, Exit Code: -2147483645\\n```\\n\\n### Testcase Gist URL\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Additional Information\\n\\n### Hardware\\n- GPU: Intel® Iris® Xe Graphics — Tiger Lake (`PCI\\\\VEN_8086&DEV_9A49`, HP subsystem `87FE103C`)\\n- Drivers tested: `31.0.101.5186` (Jan 2024) and `32.0.101.7088` (Jun 2026) — both affected\\n\\n### Diagnostics Ruled Out\\n- Hardware-Accelerated GPU Scheduling (HAGS): not enabled\\n- Hardware Shadow Stack / CET (`UserShadowStack`): NOTSET  \\n- No third-party AV or EDR (Windows Defender only)\\n- Fault offset `0x06fefb69` is deterministic across all crash attempts\\n\\n### Workaround\\n`--in-process-gpu` flag allows the app to start. `--disable-gpu` alone does **not** fix it (GPU subprocess still crashes).\\n\\n### Related Issues\\n- `electron/electron#32440` (closed — original report, different exit code `0xC0000005`)\\n- `signalapp/Signal-Desktop#5721` (open — Intel integrated graphics requiring GPU flags)\\n- `signalapp/Signal-Desktop#7828` (open — renderer crash on Windows 11)\",\n5\t \"labels\": [\n6\t  \"blocked/need-info ❌\",\n7\t  \"bug :beetle:\",\n8\t  \"platform/windows\"\n9\t ],\n10\t \"state\": \"open\",\n11\t \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n12\t \"as_of\": \"2026-09-06T02:39:33Z\",\n13\t \"replay\": true\n14\t}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e79f21cc-4ff7-4143-a911-6e1e5a923317","uuid":"a487b362-7c79-4807-a881-426cc16c15f9","timestamp":"2026-10-23T09:48:27.629Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/runner/work/cs467-electron-triage/cs467-electron-triage/.triage/issue.json","content":"{\n \"number\": 70,\n \