rocesses (e.g. Help → About window) crash with the same exit code:\\n```text\\nRender process is gone\\nError: Reason: crashed, Exit Code: -2147483645\\n```\\n\\n### Testcase Gist URL\\n\\n_No response_\\n\\n### Additional Information\\n\\n### Hardware\\n- GPU: Intel® Iris® Xe Graphics — Tiger Lake (`PCI\\\\VEN_8086&DEV_9A49`, HP subsystem `87FE103C`)\\n- Drivers tested: `31.0.101.5186` (Jan 2024) and `32.0.101.7088` (Jun 2026) — both affected\\n\\n### Diagnostics Ruled Out\\n- Hardware-Accelerated GPU Scheduling (HAGS): not enabled\\n- Hardware Shadow Stack / CET (`UserShadowStack`): NOTSET  \\n- No third-party AV or EDR (Windows Defender only)\\n- Fault offset `0x06fefb69` is deterministic across all crash attempts\\n\\n### Workaround\\n`--in-process-gpu` flag allows the app to start. `--disable-gpu` alone does **not** fix it (GPU subprocess still crashes).\\n\\n### Related Issues\\n- `electron/electron#32440` (closed — original report, different exit code `0xC0000005`)\\n- `signalapp/Signal-Desktop#5721` (open — Intel integrated graphics requiring GPU flags)\\n- `signalapp/Signal-Desktop#7828` (open — renderer crash on Windows 11)\",\n  \"form\": \"bug\",\n  \"labels_already_applied\": [\n   \"blocked/need-info ❌\",\n   \"bug :beetle:\",\n   \"platform/windows\"\n  ],\n  \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n  \"opened\": \"2026-09-06T02:39:33Z\"\n },\n \"form_fields\": {\n  \"electron_version\": \"Shipped with Signal Desktop 8.26.0 (Electron 32.x range)\",\n  \"os\": \"Windows\",\n  \"last_known_working\": \"Unknown\",\n  \"testcase_gist_url\": null\n },\n \"repro\": {\n  \"gist\": false,\n  \"other_repo_link\": false,\n  \"code_blocks\": 3\n },\n \"bot_already\": {\n  \"asked_for_supported_version\": true,\n  \"need_repro_label\": false\n },\n \"issues_linked_by_reporter\": [\n  5721,\n  7828,\n  32440\n ],\n \"component_hints\": [\n  {\n   \"label\": \"component/gpu\",\n   \"matched\": [\n    \"gpu\",\n    \"gpu process\"\n   ],\n   \"in_title\": true\n  },\n  {\n   \"label\": \"component/accessibility\",\n   \"matched\": [\n    \"aria\"\n   ],\n   \"in_title\": false\n  }\n ],\n \"redirect_hints\": {\n  \"upstream\": [\n   \"chromium\"\n  ]\n },\n \"similar_candidates\": [\n  {\n   \"number\": 52255,\n   \"opened\": \"2026-07-03\",\n   \"score\": 132.3,\n   \"title\": \"Windows 11 (build 26200) + AMD RX 9070: Chromium GPU process fails during startup (`GPU process isn't usable. Goodbye.`)\",\n   \"shared_terms\": [\n    \"signal.exe\",\n    \"defender\",\n    \"exit_code\",\n    \"-2147483645\",\n    \"x80000003\",\n    \"faulting\",\n    \"gpu_data_manager_impl_private.cc\",\n    \"0x80000003\"\n   ],\n   \"already_linked_by_reporter\": false,\n   \"excerpt\": \"### Expected Behavior Electron applications should launch normally. Maybe duplicate of : https://github.com/electron/electron/issues/52098 https://github.com/electron/electron/issues/51761 Affected applications: * Obsidian 1.12.7 * Signal Desktop 8.17.0 * Discord (latest) Not affected: * Visual Studio Code 1.126.0 ## Environment * OS: Windows 11 Pro * Build: 26200.8737 * GPU: AMD Radeon RX 9070 * \"\n  },\n  {\n   \"number\": 52098,\n   \"opened\": \"2026-06-23\",\n   \"score\": 120.6,\n   \"title\": \"GPU/renderer process crashes with EXCEPTION_BREAKPOINT (0x80000003) on Windows 11 25H2 (build 26200.8655) — sandbox init failure, regression after June 2026 cumulative update\",\n   \"shared_terms\": [\n    \"gpu_process_host.cc\",\n    \"exit_code\",\n    \"-2147483645\",\n    \"x80000003\",\n    \"faulting\",\n    \"gpu_data_manager_impl_private.cc\",\n    \"0x80000003\",\n    \"goodbye.\"\n   ],\n   \"already_linked_by_reporter\": false,\n   \"excerpt\": \"### Expected Behavior The GPU (and renderer) child process launches normally under the sandbox. ### Actual Behavior The GPU process is killed by EXCEPTION_BREAKPOINT (0x80000003 / exit_code=-2147483645) immediately on launch, **before any GPU vendor DLL is loaded**. The browser process retries 6 times within ~0.3s and then self-terminates. Browser process log (captured with --enable-logging=stderr\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"number\": 51761,\n   \"opened\": \"2026-05-24\",\n   \"score\": 103.6,\n   \"title\": \"[Bug] Electron apps crash with exit_code=-2147483645 (GPU process sandbox crash) when zombie SIDs exist in DACL\",\n   \"shared_terms\": [\n    \"hags\",\n    \"gpu_process_host.cc\",\n    \"exit_code\",\n    \"drivers\",\n    \"-2147483645\",\n    \"gpu_data_manager_impl_private.cc\",\n    \"ruled\",\n    \"goodbye.\"\n   ],\n   \"already_linked_by_reporter\": false,\n   \"excerpt\": \"### Expected Behavior Electron applications should launch normally even if the directory contains unparseable or orphaned zombie SIDs, or gracefully handle the permission validation error without crashing the entire GPU process. ### Actual Behavior The GPU process crashes on startup with exit_code=-2147483645 and outputs \\\"FATAL:gpu_data_manager_impl_private.cc: GPU process isn't usable. Goodbye.\\\" \"\n  },\n  {\n   \"number\": 51770,\n   \"opened\": \"2026-05-25\",\n   \"score\": 92.4,\n   \"title\": \"Child processes crash at launch in base::i18n::InitializeICUFromDataFile (ICU init CHECK fails), exit 0x80000003, Windows 11 26200\",\n   \"shared_terms\": [\n    \"notset\",\n    \"edr\",\n    \"status_breakpoint\",\n    \"-2147483645\",\n    \"x80000003\",\n    \"ruled\",\n    \"0x80000003\",\n    \"goodbye.\"\n   ],\n   \"already_linked_by_reporter\": false,\n   \"excerpt\": \"### Expected Behavior Electron child processes (GPU, renderer, utility) initialize and the app launches normally, as it does for Chromium/Chrome and for older-Electron apps on the same machine. ### Actual Behavior On this machine, every Electron child process aborts at the very first step of startup — before GPU init, sandbox lockdown, or logging — inside ICU initialization. The browser process is\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"number\": 52307,\n   \"opened\": \"2026-07-12\",\n   \"score\": 76.0,\n   \"title\": \"App crashes with RENDERER GONE: crashed -1073741819 and no other console output when locales/ directory is empty\",\n   \"shared_terms\": [\n    \"status_access_violation\",\n    \"xc0000005\",\n    \"surfaces\",\n    \"0xc0000005\",\n    \"gone\",\n    \"attempts\",\n    \"silently\",\n    \"exit\"\n   ],\n   \"already_linked_by_reporter\": false,\n   \"excerpt\": \"### Expected Behavior When no locale data is available for the app's target locale, Electron should either log a clear diagnostic (e.g. `Error: No locale file found for \\\"en\\\"`) before the renderer fails, or surface a specific reason via `render-process-gone` — not fail silently with only a bare exit code. ### Actual Behavior The app crashes on launch with only this single line printed to console: `\"\n  }\n ],\n \"similar_search\": \"BM25 over issue-corpus.jsonl, only issues opened before 2026-09-06T02:39:33Z\"\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01KmqBG4kE5fnR3twX8yrjrd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
